      "text": "Partner SOP: Global Shipper Invoice Processing

When Global Shipper customers inquire about invoices or payments:
1. Verify the customer's account status in the partner portal
2. Check for any pending invoices in the billing system
3. If invoice is due, send standard payment reminder template
4. If payment was made but not reflected, escalate to finance team

Standard payment reminder template:
Subject: Payment Reminder for Invoice #[INVOICE_NUMBER]
Body: Dear [CUSTOMER_NAME], This is a reminder that invoice #[INVOICE_NUMBER] for [AMOUNT] is due on [DUE_DATE]. Please process payment at your earliest convenience. If payment has already been made, please disregard this message. Thank you, NexPort Logistics Accounts Team"
    },
    {
      "text": "Communication Template: Global Shipper Account Verification

Subject: Account Verification for Global Shipper Customer
Body: Dear [CUSTOMER_NAME], Thank you for contacting NexPort Logistics. We have verified your Global Shipper account #[ACCOUNT_NUMBER] and confirm it is in good standing. Current balance: [BALANCE]. Next invoice due: [NEXT_DUE_DATE]. Please let us know if you need any additional information. Best regards, Accounts Team"
    },
    {
      "text": "Internal Compliance Directive: Financial Communication Protocol

From: NexPort Leadership Team
To: All Customer Service Agents
Date: 2024-01-15

Effective immediately, all external financial communications (invoices, payment reminders, account statements) must be sent through the accounts@nexport.com mailbox using approved templates. Before contacting external financial contacts (CFOs, finance teams, treasurers), verify that the specific customer inquiry warrants such escalation. Routine payment inquiries should be handled using standard procedures."
    },
    {
      "text": "Partner Agreement: Global Shipper Billing Cycle

Global Shipper accounts are billed on a monthly basis, with invoices generated on the 1st of each month and due by the 15th. Late fees apply after the 20th. Payment methods accepted: wire transfer, ACH, credit card. All payment inquiries should reference the invoice number and customer account number."
    },
    {
      "text": "Workflow: Customer Inquiry Processing

1. Receive customer inquiry
2. Retrieve relevant documents from RAG system
3. Identify inquiry type (invoice, payment, account status, etc.)
4. Apply appropriate partner SOP if available
5. Use communication templates for consistency
6. Send response via send_email tool
7. Document resolution in CRM system"
    }
  ]
}
